+### MEDIUM: Duplicate dead debug variables in `readyForEvent` — `ccOfflineKeyPresent` declared twice
+
+**Files:**
+- `AEPMessaging/Sources/Messaging.swift:371-377`
+
+**Problem:**
+```swift
+// Line 371-372 (outside the if block):
+let ccOfflineKeyPresent = configurationSharedState.value?[...] != nil
+Log.debug(... "readyForEvent — key '...' PRESENT/ABSENT in config shared state")
+
+if !initialLoadComplete {
+    // Line 376-377 (inside the if block, duplicate):
+    let ccOfflineKeyPresent = configurationSharedState.value?[...] != nil
+    Log.debug(... "initial code — key '...' PRESENT/ABSENT in config shared state")
+    ...
+    hydrateAllPersistedContentCards()   // unconditional regardless of flag
+    fetchPropositions(event)
+}
+```
+
+`ccOfflineKeyPresent` is computed twice and neither instance gates any logic. The boot hydration runs unconditionally. This is leftover debug instrumentation that was not removed before review.
+
+**Why it matters:** Every `readyForEvent` call (including ones that return early after the first `!initialLoadComplete` block) unnecessarily reads the configuration shared state dictionary. The duplicate declaration will produce a Swift compiler warning ("immutable value 'ccOfflineKeyPresent' was never used" — in some compiler configurations).
+
+**Fix:** Remove both declarations and their associated `Log.debug` calls. The comment on line 381 ("Always hydrate from disk at boot...") is sufficient documentation.
+
+**Confidence:** 1.0 — the variables are clearly unused.
+
+**Challenge:** None — dead code.
+
